This suite verifies that mgr/volumes' auto-upgrade of pre-v3 (v1 and v2)
subvolumes to the v3 layout is non-disruptive across a Ceph upgrade.

Starting from an N-1|N-2 release, the setup step creates, with all the
subvolumes below (except clones and purges) being either v1 or v2 (the
3-setup facet):

  - 3 subvolumes, each mounted by a dedicated client (a mix of kernel and
    ceph-fuse) using subvolume-scoped credentials, with a background writer
    continuously doing IO in it. Two of them get snapshots (one and two)
    taken while their clients are writing.
  - 3 async clones (from a snapshot of a separate source subvolume, which
    has two snapshots) that are caught mid-copy and paused
    (mgr/volumes/pause_cloning). The clones themselves are v2, as the old
    ceph-mgr creates them so.
  - 3 subvolume purges (`fs subvolume rm`) of v2 subvolumes that are caught
    mid-purge and paused (mgr/volumes/pause_purging). The old ceph-mgr
    upgrades a v1 subvolume to v2 before removing it, so there are no v1
    purges.

v2 subvolumes are created through `fs subvolume create`, and their
credentials through `fs subvolume authorize`. No release that can be
upgraded from creates v1 subvolumes, so they are fabricated in the layout
ceph-mgr used to create them in (data and v1 snapshots in
<subvolume>/<uuid>, .meta with version 1), with credentials for the data
dir. The first snapshot of a v1 subvolume is taken directly in its data dir,
the rest through the old ceph-mgr, which must handle it as v1. A v1
subvolume without snapshots is not accessed through the old ceph-mgr, which
would upgrade it to v2.

The cluster is then upgraded, either:

  - mgr-only first: the new ceph-mgr can't auto-upgrade subvolumes as the old
    MDS does not know the `ceph.dir.subvolume.prevpath` vxattr. The v1/v2
    subvolumes must keep working as such (except for a v1 subvolume without
    snapshots possibly getting upgraded to v2, as ceph-mgr always did):
    client IO and subvolume commands (getpath, info, snapshot
    create/ls/info, clone status) must succeed, and the clones and purges
    must finish. The remaining daemons are upgraded afterwards.
  - full: all daemons in one go.

After the upgrade, the first subvolume command on each subvolume must upgrade
it to v3 in place, keeping its uuid whether or not it has snapshots, while
its client keeps doing IO uninterrupted and without having to remount. The
clones and purges started before the upgrade must finish successfully (for
v1, while the clone source, and the snapshot being cloned with it, gets
upgraded). Snapshot listing must include the snapshots taken before (v1/v2)
and after (v3) the auto-upgrade, and new clones of v1/v2 snapshots must work
(both with only ceph-mgr upgraded and after the full upgrade), with data
matching the snapshot.

Finally, each client is remounted at its subvolume's new v3 path twice: with
the credentials it had been using (for the v1/v2 data dir), and with new ones
from `fs subvolume authorize` after the upgrade (which must be for the v3
path). Each time, all the data written by it must be accessible and intact,
and the subvolume must be writable.

This suite should make use of N-1|N-2 releases.
